I achieved my development objective of becoming proficient in Apache Spark and Databricks using Python. I demonstrated that proficiency by designing and implementing data processing solutions for CubIQ, including direct access to MRV calculations and automated reconciliation.

For OneRisk, I designed and implemented a solution that exposes MRV results directly from CubIQ Delta tables through Databricks Metric Views. I developed Spark notebooks to transform the input data used by the Metric Views. The new query path enabled OneRisk to complete its data loads within the agreed SLA and reduced demand on the shared Power BI semantic model.

I also designed and implemented the Spark-based processing engine behind the CubIQ MRV reconciliation dashboard. The engine loads and compares batches of calculation results across data layers, including the on-premises baseline, and produces a consolidated report for the dashboard. This supported daily reconciliation across approximately 2,500 MRV calculations and helped the team identify discrepancies earlier and verify fixes against the agreed acceptance criteria.

My next development objective is to build comparable hands-on proficiency in Microsoft Fabric. I plan to apply what I learned from these projects to a CubIQ use case, focusing on data ingestion and transformation, semantic model integration, and performance validation.
